      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T18:12:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you know why that happens? Wouldn\u0027t you expect the initial state of a test case to be disconnected?\n\n\u003e and allows time for asynchronous disconnect debounce to settle\n\nFor the purposes of these tests (and most tests), this operation ought to be synchronous. It looks like we have `disconnect_source_from_port` and `disconnect_sink_from_port` for that purpose. You could use `disconnect_source_from_port` here to replace several individual operations.",
      "parentUuid": "7b2dd8b8_3c17a1c0",
      "revId": "24d41c8acf2cd84654065e4013ffda86cb135586",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
